# extension -> language, one pair per line (HLR-060).
#
# This is data, not code. Associating another extension with a language, or
# pointing an extension at a different language, is an edit here and needs no
# rebuild. Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored; the
# extension may be written with or without its leading period, and is matched
# without regard to case.
#
# An extension absent from this file maps to no language, and a file carrying
# it is skipped and reported as skipped (HLR-012) — not an error.

# C. Headers map to C as well: a header carries function definitions in
# practice (static inline, and anything a single-header library ships), and
# an unmapped .h would be reported skipped on almost every C project.
.c    c
.h    c

# C++, Rust, Python, and Ada arrive with their grammars in Phase 6 (HLR-011).
